614	447	569	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Best practice is to run backups on the AG secondary to offload the primary. However, backup I/O (especially full backups) can compete with redo I/O. If the secondary has limited I/O bandwidth, running a full backup during peak write hours on the primary can cause redo to fall behind. Mitigations: (1) schedule secondary backups during low-write periods, (2) use backup compression to reduce I/O, (3) set MAXTRANSFERSIZE/BUFFERCOUNT for optimal throughput, (4) use Resource Governor (Enterprise) to limit backup I/O, (5) ensure the secondary has sufficient I/O bandwidth for both redo and backup.	2026-02-23 20:18:31.870168
