616	448	571	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	After a secondary replica restart, two factors compound redo lag: (1) accumulated log during downtime must be redone, (2) the buffer pool is empty so every page redo needs a disk read first. SQL Server 2016+ supports buffer pool extension and buffer pool scan optimization. SQL Server 2012+ has sys.dm_os_buffer_pool_extension_configuration. To warm the buffer pool faster: (1) use 'buffer pool scan' feature in newer SQL versions, (2) pre-warm by running representative queries, (3) SQL Server 2019+ has hybrid buffer pool for persistent memory. The redo lag should decrease as the buffer pool warms up — if it persists after 30+ minutes, investigate other causes.	2026-02-23 20:18:31.870169
