948	603	898	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Auto-shrink on tempdb is one of the worst SQL Server misconfigurations. Tempdb shrinks during low activity, then must auto-grow again during peak — causing file I/O stalls, physical file fragmentation, and wasted I/O. Auto-shrink also causes index fragmentation because pages are moved during shrink. Fix: ALTER DATABASE tempdb SET AUTO_SHRINK OFF. Never shrink tempdb manually either — instead restart SQL Server if tempdb is too large (tempdb is recreated on restart). Step 2 on_no_match still confirms because auto-shrink being enabled is the problem regardless of whether events have been captured.	2026-02-23 20:18:31.870377
