2913	1515	2849	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Periodic access reviews are a fundamental security control (SOX, PCI-DSS, HIPAA all require them). Evidence of reviews: (1) logins regularly disabled or removed, (2) permission modifications on existing accounts, (3) audit trail of role membership changes, (4) scheduled jobs generating permission reports. In SQL Server, the absence of disabled logins is a strong signal — if no accounts have ever been disabled, no review has occurred. Fix: (1) implement quarterly access review process, (2) enable SERVER_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP and DATABASE_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP in audit, (3) create a scheduled report of all permissions using sys.server_role_members, sys.database_role_members, and sys.database_permissions.	2026-02-23 20:18:31.871639
