3417	1778	3347	1	next	\N	next	\N	SQL Server encryption functions (DECRYPTBYKEY, DECRYPTBYCERT, DECRYPTBYPASSPHRASE, ENCRYPTBYPASSPHRASE) take sensitive data as parameters. When statement-level XE events or Query Store capture these calls, the function parameters (including passphrases and plaintext data) persist in event files or query store tables. sp_executesql calls with sensitive parameters are similarly exposed. The risk is highest with ad-hoc queries using DECRYPTBYPASSPHRASE where the passphrase appears as a literal string in the query text.	2026-02-23 20:18:31.872043
