3425	1782	3355	1	next	\N	next	\N	SQL Server ERRORLOG is cycled on service restart or by running sp_cycle_errorlog. Without a scheduled job to cycle the log, it grows indefinitely until the next restart. The 'number of errorlog files' setting (default: 6) controls how many archived logs are kept. With the default, only 6 rotations are retained — but if the server runs for months without cycling, the current ERRORLOG can become very large. Log files contain: failed login attempts (with usernames), error messages (with query context), and audit events. Best practice: create a SQL Agent job running sp_cycle_errorlog weekly, set retention to 12-14 files, and ensure OS-level ACLs restrict log directory access.	2026-02-23 20:18:31.872048
